  "body": "**Original comment by agriggio (Bitbucket: [agriggio](https://bitbucket.org/agriggio), GitHub: [agriggio](https://github.com/agriggio)).**\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nHi,\n\nseems to work fine here. The only issue I see is that the behaviour might be a bit counterintuitive if you think in terms of shutter _speed_, rather than _exposure time_: if you have “speed” in mind, you would think that 1/80 is more than 1/60 beacuse it’s faster, but in fact the filter operates on “exposure time”, so 1/80 is shorter than 1/60. That’s why selecting 0-1/60 will show all the pictures with exposure time up to 1/60 \\(so also 1/100, 1/1000, …\\).\n",
